    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The gentle call of spring weather drew more border crossers to the U.S. border, with apprehensions surging from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March—a rising tide of human connection seeking to happen. Yet this seasonal increase belies a deeper pattern: crossings remain at historic lows, a maintained separation enforced by strict asylum shutdown and deportation policies. Observers note the tension between those caught in the boundary's grasp and the security force tasked with apprehending them.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Lover",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "who-1",
        "center_kind": "who",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 0
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.65
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Despite the numerical change showing increased border activity along the southwest border, enforcement policy outcome keeps year-to-date crossings near multi-decade lows. This maintained separation, deep and long-standing, reflects a failure to find common ground among government officials, who remain deadlocked over separate funding for immigration enforcement agencies in a pending reconciliation package. The political deadlock on funding underscores a profound impasse where the power to unite or divide lies unresolved.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Lover",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "center": "result-0",
        "center_kind": "result",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.55
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A growing rupture in the boundary's fabric appeared as a surge in border crossings marked by the increase in apprehensions from February to March. Policy observers and security analysts watch as souls crossing the divide meet a border security agency enforcing policies that maintain low crossing numbers. Meanwhile, deadlocked legislators fail to bridge the funding dispute, leaving the geographic region caught between desire for connection and the reality of enforced separation.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Lover",
